drm/amd/display: tiled-stitch layer for Apple 5K iMac panels (on top of the lean core)

Optional layer that applies ON TOP of imac5k-lean-core-7.2.x.patch. It is
erik2's single-display stitch (unchanged, logging intact): the kernel exposes
the two 2560x2880 tiles as one 5120x2880 output on the eDP connector and drives
the DP slave tile as the root crtc's peer stream, marked non-desktop. Needed
only for compositors without tile support (Hyprland). Mutter stitches on its
own; KWin is getting there; upstream will not take this layer, the lean core
is the mainline candidate.

Adds the module parameter amdgpu.tiled_stitch (-1 auto, 0 off, 1 on).

Also carries the two stitch-specific boot fixes from this repo, unchanged:
  * early modeset: a second drm_client_dev_hotplug() after drm_client_setup()
    so the peer tile stream exists before Plymouth draws the disk-password
    prompt (otherwise the right half is dark for ~1 s);
  * settle-and-resync: re-run the timing sync 250 ms after each commit that
    touches the tiled pair, because the one-shot alignment can fire before the
    re-trained slave tile is running.

One fix over erik2's original: the saved tile-group id buffer was 8 bytes
while DRM tile-group ids (drm_tile_group.group_data, and the topology_id
argument of drm_mode_get/create_tile_group) are 9 bytes. The restore path
copied a truncated id and the lookup read one byte past the buffer, so a
restored slave connector could end up in a fresh, mismatched tile group.
Now 9 bytes (gcc flagged it: -Wstringop-overread).

Apply order on a pristine 7.1.x / 7.2.x tree:
  patch -p1 < patches/imac5k-lean-core-7.2.x.patch
  patch -p1 < patches/imac5k-stitch-layer-7.x.patch

Not-Yet-Signed-off-by: mr_projects
